## Verify this release

Every release file is listed in `checksums.txt`, which is signed keyless by `release.yml` at `{{TAG}}`. The guide [Verify releases](https://github.com/{{REPOSITORY}}/blob/{{TAG}}/docs/security/verify-releases.md) explains each step.

```bash
gh release download {{TAG}} --repo {{REPOSITORY}} --pattern 'checksums.txt*' --pattern '{{UPDATER_ASSET_LINUX_AMD64}}'
cosign verify-blob --bundle checksums.txt.sigstore.json \
  --certificate-identity '{{IDENTITY}}' \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer {{OIDC_ISSUER}} checksums.txt
sha256sum --check --ignore-missing checksums.txt
gh attestation verify {{UPDATER_ASSET_LINUX_AMD64}} --repo {{REPOSITORY}} --signer-workflow {{SIGNER_WORKFLOW}} --source-ref refs/tags/{{TAG}}
gh release verify {{TAG}} --repo {{REPOSITORY}}
gh release verify-asset {{TAG}} checksums.txt --repo {{REPOSITORY}}
cosign verify {{SERVER_IMAGE}}@{{SERVER_DIGEST}} \
  --certificate-identity '{{IDENTITY}}' --certificate-oidc-issuer {{OIDC_ISSUER}}
cosign verify {{UPDATER_IMAGE}}@{{UPDATER_DIGEST}} \
  --certificate-identity '{{IDENTITY}}' --certificate-oidc-issuer {{OIDC_ISSUER}}
gh attestation verify oci://{{SERVER_IMAGE}}@{{SERVER_DIGEST}} --repo {{REPOSITORY}} --bundle-from-oci --signer-workflow {{SIGNER_WORKFLOW}} --source-ref refs/tags/{{TAG}}
```

Use gh 2.102.0 or newer: older versions treat `--signer-workflow ...@refs/tags/<tag>` as a prefix, and `--source-ref` is the exact check in every version. `gh release verify`, `gh release verify-asset` and the online `gh attestation verify` need a login (`gh auth login` or `GH_TOKEN`). `cosign verify` of an image also accepts the attestations of the same identity; the JSON entry of the type `https://sigstore.dev/cosign/sign/v1` is the cosign signature. `gh release verify-asset` (membership of a file in this immutable release) is the proof that a file was released.

The build provenance is also the release file `{{PROVENANCE_ASSET}}` (`gh attestation verify <file> --bundle {{PROVENANCE_ASSET}} --repo {{REPOSITORY}}` needs no call to the attestation API; offline it needs a trusted root that gh cached within the last day, or `--custom-trusted-root`, see the section "Offline and behind a proxy" of the guide). The installers check `checksums.txt` against the version-bound pattern `{{IDENTITY_BOUND_REGEXP}}`; the pattern for any release is `{{IDENTITY_REGEXP}}`.

